# Extrapolate the Impossible: "You may reveal exactly two cards you own with different names from outside the game."
# Bot1 owns two Lightning Bolts and a Counterspell outside the game. Either Bolt can be the first card revealed (each has
# the Counterspell to pair with), but once one is revealed the other Bolt is not a card of a different name, so it is not
# offered for the second card (CR 608.2d: the reveal is exactly two cards of different names, and an illegal choice is
# never offered). Bot2 then names the Bolt, which comes into Bot1's hand; the Counterspell stays outside the game.

[Bot1 Deck]
Extrapolate the Impossible
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Island
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Extrapolate the Impossible.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
! Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Choose(Counterspell)
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Lightning Bolt; Swamp; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Sideboard = Lightning Bolt; Counterspell
Bot1.Graveyard = Extrapolate the Impossible
Stack.Count = 0
